IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- INFORMATION AND EVIDENCE TO BE FURNISHED (regulations 52 to 54.1).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 499 to 574.
--
-- Five lists of what an applicant or beneficiary must set out or furnish to the Minister: for any benefit (52), for the
-- months of a family allowance recipient (53), for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings (54(1)) and the
-- information relating to the marriage (54(2)), and for an assignment of a retirement pension (54.1).
-- Each list is an enumeration in cr2-nouns.l4. The text says each item is required "as is applicable" (or "such of the
-- following ... as is applicable") and never says when an item applies, so the items that apply are an input (fork F-46).
-- The duty falls due "in the application, or thereafter in writing when requested to do so by the Minister": a rule
-- therefore answers "what is still to be set out or furnished", and the answer is empty until the application is made or
-- the Minister has asked in writing. Regulations 54(3) and 54.1(2) let the Minister ask for an original certificate.

§ `Part V -- Information and evidence required to be furnished (regulations 52 to 54.1)`

§§ `Regulation 52 -- any benefit`

-- src:500 | 52 For the purposes of determining the eligibility of an applicant for a benefit, the amount that an applicant or beneficiary is entitled to receive as a benefit or the eligibility of a beneficiary to continue to receive a benefit, the applicant, the person applying on his behalf, or the beneficiary, as the case may be, shall, in the application, or thereafter in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, set out or furnish the Minister with the following applicable information or evidence:
-- src:501 | (a) the name at birth and present name, sex, address and Social Insurance Number of
-- src:502 | (i) the applicant or beneficiary,
-- src:503 | (ii) the disabled or deceased contributor,
-- src:504 | (iii) the spouse or common-law partner of the disabled contributor or the survivor of the deceased contributor,
-- src:505 | (iv) each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor, and
-- src:506 | (v) any former spouse or former common-law partner, where known to the applicant;
-- src:507 | (b) the date and place of birth of
-- src:508 | (i) the applicant or beneficiary,
-- src:509 | (ii) the disabled or deceased contributor,
-- src:510 | (iii) the survivor of the deceased contributor, and
-- src:511 | (iv) each dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor;
-- src:512 | (c) the date and place of death of the contributor;
-- src:513 | (d) whether a dependent child of the contributor has died since
-- src:514 | (i) the date on which the contributor claims to have become disabled, or
-- src:515 | (ii) the death of the contributor;
-- src:516 | (e) [Repealed, SOR/86-1133, s. 10]
-- src:517 | (f) whether the deceased contributor was married at the time of his death and, if so, to whom, and the date and place of the marriage;
-- src:518 | (g) whether the deceased contributor was separated or divorced at the time of his death;
-- src:519 | (h) whether there is a personal representative of the estate of the deceased contributor, and the name and address of any such personal representative;
-- src:520 | (i) whether a dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor
-- src:521 | (i) is his child,
-- src:522 | (ii) is his legally adopted child or was adopted in fact by him or is a legally adopted child of another person,
-- src:523 | (iii) was a child, in respect of whom, either legally or in fact, the contributor had parenting time or decision-making responsibility,
-- src:524 | (iv) is a child, in respect of whom, the disabled contributor, the survivor of the contributor or another person or agency had decision-making responsibility,
-- src:525 | (v) [Repealed, SOR/2024-265, s. 3]
-- src:526 | (vi) is or was maintained by the disabled contributor;
-- src:527 | (j) if a dependent child of the disabled or deceased contributor is 18 or more years of age, whether that child is or was in full-time or part-time attendance at a school or university;
-- src:528 | (k) whether the applicant or beneficiary who is the survivor of a contributor maintains wholly or substantially one or more dependent children of the deceased contributor;
-- src:529 | (k.1) [Repealed, SOR/2013-83, s. 2]
-- src:530 | (l) a statement evidencing the amount of the contributory salary and wages and of the contributory self-employed earnings of a disabled or deceased contributor for the year in which the contributor became disabled or died and for any preceding year;
-- src:531 | (m) whether the applicant, beneficiary or deceased contributor is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan or a pension under the Old Age Security Act; and
-- src:532 | (n) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of the applicant or beneficiary or are obtainable by him that will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (m).
@ref Reg 52 (src:500-532)
GIVEN `the application is being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 52`
      `the items already set out or furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 52`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 52`
`reg 52 — the items the applicant or beneficiary still has to set out or furnish`
    `the application is being made`
    `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    `the items that are applicable`
    `the items already set out or furnished` MEANS
    IF `the application is being made` OR `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    THEN filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already set out or furnished`)) `the items that are applicable`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Regulation 53 -- months of a family allowance recipient`

-- src:533 | 53 For the purposes of determining whether any months during which a contributor was a family allowance recipient should not be included in his contributory period, the applicant shall, in the application or thereafter in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, set out or furnish the Minister with such of the following additional information or evidence as is applicable:
-- src:534 | (a) the name and date of birth of all children in respect of whom the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits;
-- src:535 | (b) the Social Insurance Number, if any, of each of those children;
-- src:536 | (c) the periods during which the contributor received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children;
-- src:537 | (d) the province in which the contributor resided while in receipt of family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children;
-- src:538 | (e) the Social Insurance Number of the contributor to whom family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits were paid in respect of those children;
-- src:539 | (f) if known, the name and Social Insurance Number of any other person who received family allowance benefits or Canada child benefits in respect of those children; and
-- src:540 | (g) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of the applicant or are obtainable by him that will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (f).
@ref Reg 53 (src:533-540)
GIVEN `the application is being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 53`
      `the items already set out or furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 53`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 53`
`reg 53 — the items the applicant still has to set out or furnish about family allowance months`
    `the application is being made`
    `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    `the items that are applicable`
    `the items already set out or furnished` MEANS
    IF `the application is being made` OR `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    THEN filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already set out or furnished`)) `the items that are applicable`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Regulation 54(1) -- a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings`

-- src:541 | 54 (1) For the purpose of determining whether an application for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c) of the Act may be approved, the applicant must, set out in the application, or furnish in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, the information required under section 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require, as well as the following information or evidence, as is applicable:
-- src:542 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner;
-- src:543 | (b) the date and place of birth of each spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner;
-- src:544 | (c) whether the spouse, former spouse or former common-law partner is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan;
-- src:545 | (d) the date and place of marriage of the spouses or former spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:546 | (e) the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage of the former spouses;
-- src:547 | (f) documentary evidence of any such dissolution of marriage, including the decree absolute of divorce, the judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act, or the judgment of nullity;
-- src:548 | (g) the address of all residences where the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners lived together;
-- src:549 | (h) the dates of any periods when the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:550 | (i) the date that the spouses, former spouses or former common- law partners commenced to live separate and apart;
-- src:551 | (j) the dates of all periods when the spouses, former spouses or former common-law partners lived together in a conjugal relationship;
-- src:552 | (k) a copy of any written agreement between persons subject to a division that was entered into before June 4, 1986 or any written agreement between such persons that was entered into on or after that date and contains a provision that is binding on the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act; and
-- src:553 | (l) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of, or are obtainable by, the applicant as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (k).
@ref Reg 54(1) (src:541-553)
GIVEN `the application is being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)`
      `the items already set out or furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54(1)`
`reg 54(1) — the items the applicant still has to set out or furnish for a division`
    `the application is being made`
    `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    `the items that are applicable`
    `the items already set out or furnished` MEANS
    IF `the application is being made` OR `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    THEN filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already set out or furnished`)) `the items that are applicable`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Regulation 54(2) -- the information relating to the marriage`

-- src:554 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph 55.1(1)(a) of the Act, the information relating to the marriage is the following, as is applicable:
-- src:555 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of each of the former spouses;
-- src:556 | (b) the date and place of marriage of the former spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:557 | (c) the date and place of the dissolution of the marriage of the former spouses;
-- src:558 | (d) a copy of the decree or judgment referred to in that paragraph;
-- src:559 | (e) the addresses of all residences where the former spouses lived together;
-- src:560 | (f) the dates of any periods when the former spouses did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:561 | (g) the date that the former spouses commenced to live separate and apart;
-- src:562 | (h) the dates of all periods when the former spouses lived together in a conjugal relationship; and
-- src:563 | (i) a copy of any written agreement between persons subject to a division that was entered into before June 4, 1986 or any written agreement between such persons that was entered into on or after that date and contains a provision that is binding on the Minister under subsection 55.2(3) of the Act.
@ref Reg 54(2) (src:554-563)
GIVEN `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information relating to the marriage under regulation 54(2)`
      `the items already provided` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information relating to the marriage under regulation 54(2)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information relating to the marriage under regulation 54(2)`
`reg 54(2) — the information relating to the marriage that is still lacking` `the items that are applicable` `the items already provided` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already provided`)) `the items that are applicable`

-- 54(3) and 54.1(2) are the same power: the Minister may require the original certificate of marriage, or a copy of the
-- act of marriage issued by the competent authority, where there are reasonable grounds to doubt the copy.
-- src:564 | (3) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage referred to in paragraph (1)(d) or (2)(b), the Minister may require that the original certificate of marriage or, if applicable, a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority be furnished.
@ref Reg 54(3) (src:564)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 54(3) — the Minister may require the original certificate of marriage or a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority`
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage`

§§ `Regulation 54.1(1) -- an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension`

-- src:565 | 54.1 (1) For the purpose of determining whether an application for an assignment of a portion of a retirement pension under section 65.1 of the Act may be approved, the applicant must set out in the application, or furnish in writing when requested to do so by the Minister, the information required under section 52, with any modifications that the circumstances require, as well as the following information or evidence, as is applicable:
-- src:566 | (a) the name at birth and present name, the sex, address and Social Insurance Number of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:567 | (b) the date and place of birth of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner;
-- src:568 | (c) whether the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner is or was in receipt of or has applied for a benefit under the Act or under a provincial pension plan;
-- src:569 | (d) the date and place of marriage of the spouses and their certificate of marriage, a copy of that certificate or a copy of their act of marriage;
-- src:570 | (e) the month in which the spouses or common-law partners commenced to live together in a conjugal relationship;
-- src:571 | (f) the dates of any periods when the spouses or common-law partners did not live together and whether the separations or any of them were for any reason set out in paragraph 78(2)(a) or subsection 78.1(3);
-- src:572 | (g) documentary evidence of the dissolution of any previous marriage of the applicant, including the decree absolute of divorce, the judgment granting a divorce under the Divorce Act or the judgment of nullity; and
-- src:573 | (h) such additional documents, statements or records that are in the possession of, or are obtainable by, the applicant as will assist the Minister in ascertaining the accuracy of the information and evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) to (g).
@ref Reg 54.1(1) (src:565-573)
GIVEN `the application is being made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the items that are applicable` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54.1(1)`
      `the items already set out or furnished` IS A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54.1(1)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cr2 Item of information or evidence under regulation 54.1(1)`
`reg 54.1(1) — the items the applicant still has to set out or furnish for an assignment`
    `the application is being made`
    `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    `the items that are applicable`
    `the items already set out or furnished` MEANS
    IF `the application is being made` OR `the Minister has requested the information or evidence in writing`
    THEN filter (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (elem item `the items already set out or furnished`)) `the items that are applicable`
    ELSE EMPTY

-- src:574 | (2) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage referred to in paragraph (1)(d), the Minister may require that the original certificate of marriage or, if applicable, a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority be furnished.
@ref Reg 54.1(2) (src:574)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 54.1(2) — the Minister may require the original certificate of marriage or a copy of the act of marriage issued by the competent authority`
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a certificate or act of marriage` MEANS
